{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490552-fairy-stricken-another-form-of-fairy-kidnapping","id":1490552,"title":"fairy stricken / another form of fairy kidnapping","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-17T15:37:20-07:00","id":1490552,"title":"fairy stricken / another form of fairy kidnapping","content":"This is a companion to my post of fairy stocks/fetches <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488496-fairy-stocks-fetches\">here</a>. Another way for fairies to abduct people was not by kidnapping them physically, but ensnaring their souls or minds.<br /> <br /> There is lots of folklore of people being in some kind of immobile, comatose, or sickened state as having been taking by the fairies. But they didn't believe the sick, immobile person had been replaced. They believed the person's body was still there, but their mind had been transplanted into the fairy world where it was now trapped. (The medical term &quot;stroke&quot; in fact is derived from a person being &quot;elf struck&quot;.)<br /> <br /> This is also seen in a different degree in the book and BBC miniseries Jonathon Strange a &amp; Mr Norrel where Lady Pole is forced to attend fairy balls every night during her sleep, a process that gradually wastes her from exhaustion since she can never get rest.<br /> <br /> What would be a good way to emulate that? Now in the Enchanted rules, we do learn that enchanted humans who spend too much time in the Dreaming can become dream struck and fall into coma, but that isn't this. I've also used the term fairy stricken or association with actual strokes and similar medical trauma to describe the process of the Chrysalis, especially for Wilders and Grumps who change late. This is just a way for the fae to somehow take a person's soul or mind, incarnate in a (likely chimerical, but identical) body to serve them in the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> This is certainly something that should be beyond any normal Arts. But I can't think of some general mechanics that can emulate it, but have sufficient limitations that fairies just can't do it everyone. It should be relatively rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T18:12:12-07:00","id":1490662,"title":"","content":"I don't think it would actually be beyond normal Arts, at least in scope, and it would probably be a fairly reasonable Unleashing of Oneiromancy. By itself that would make this power something many Changelings wouldn't do without reason.<br /> <br /> The greater problems, instead of the difficulty at just doing it, would be the consequences to the Dreaming, depending on who the Fae are targeting. I'd make it equivalent to Ravaging, except instead of requiring a connection it requires the Unleashing. If the Changeling fails either the Unleashing or the subsequent Banality roll, they gain Banality as per the Ravaging rules. The mortal won't feel the effects of Ravaging until they leave the Dreaming, so during their stay other Changelings can further Ravage them, too. Sending a high Banality mortal is also a Banality Trigger, as their Chimerical body is still just as Banal as normal and run the risk of corrupting the Dreaming, however you run this risk.<br /> <br /> Also, as a human soul trapped within a Chimera, this mortal now follow the rules on Chimera, and being the Dreaming what it is, the ST has a lot of leeway into making whatever they want with this new Banal Chimera until it leaves the Dreaming, and loosing control of the Unleashing means losing track of where this Chimera will manifest or it stats or Redes. Specifics aren't needed here at this point. Tales of mortals returning from the Dreaming far older than they used to be may come from such situations. Whatever this Chimera does, the Changeling responsible may be held accountable in some form.<br /> <br /> Now we have many reasons for this to be rare, even if the payback is good enough for some to try. You risk up to two points of Banality even if you use Willpower to guarantee not getting a dot, one of them being more likely than normal to come, you risk Nightmare by the Unleashing, it costs Glamour, if it backfires you have to track this mortal somewhere in the Dreaming with them possibly becoming hard to find or more dangerous than you thought. Heck, the mortal may even end up in the Deep Dreaming as they're now a Chimera, even if they're not only un-enchanted, but also with whatever Banality rating they have.<br /> <br /> Probably affecting the mortal with Arts now requires Fae. At least 3, but I would raise it to 4 or even 5, as the mortal-made-Chimera isn't any other Chimera, but a really strange entity, making dealing with them even harder however this ends up coming (at the same time still requires Actor as normal, just in case you think outsourcing Fae will solve your problems easily).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T23:40:16-07:00","id":1490680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490552-fairy-stricken-another-form-of-fairy-kidnapping?p=1490662#post1490662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it would actually be beyond normal Arts, at least in scope, and it would probably be a fairly reasonable Unleashing of Oneiromancy. By itself that would make this power something many Changelings wouldn't do without reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know about the Art of Oneiromancy so thanks for the information. I have limited sourcebooks for Changeling so I was unaware of it. But I did look it up in the White Wolf Wiki after your post. I agree that it is a strong possibility to emulate the concept. <br /> <br /> No powers directly match, but it's easy enough to create a variant of Expiation. Their real body falls into coma or some other dreamlike state, while their mind/soul manifests in the Dreaming in a chimerical body. And as a forbidden art, it'd be easy to keep it in limited use. And the mechanics you suggest makes sense to me. I like the ties to Ravaging, it provides a real reason why fae would want to do this, and fits the terrible effects on a person.<br /> <br /> I am not familiar with the term &quot;Unleashing&quot;. What exactly does it mean? Is it a term I just did not pay attention to? Or is it from C20 or some obscure sourcebook?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T03:06:21-07:00","id":1490691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490552-fairy-stricken-another-form-of-fairy-kidnapping?p=1490680#post1490680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not familiar with the term &quot;Unleashing&quot;. What exactly does it mean? Is it a term I just did not pay attention to? Or is it from C20 or some obscure sourcebook?</div> </div> </div> </div>C20. I really recommend you take it up, even if just the core, despite (and because of) how much it changes some rules (CtD badly needed a <i>Revised</i> and never got one, so it's it and did it well).<br /> <br /> Put shortly, Unleashing is a special action where you call directly on the Dreaming for an improvised effect based on an Art you have at least one dot. With it you can make almost anything withing the thematic scope of the Art, but you give up <b>a lot of </b>control. Not only does it let all the details in the hands of the Dreaming/ST, if you get more successes than your rank in the Art things go out of control royally.<br /> <br /> Nightmare is a mechanic that taints your Arts and gives you even more dice for Unleashing (Glamour + Nightmare, up to 20 dice), but when it overflows it taints your Willpower and may end up in Bedlam (so it finally has mechanics for it). Unleashing always give you Nightmare, so this rule may give you both risks.<br /> <br /> For a 2nd ed take use Ravaging rules, +1 Banality if the mortal is Banal, and the source may be a secret Oneiromancy variation, an Art of its own, a Treasure, or even a specialized Rede. The increased risk of Bedlam stays as a prescriptive mental note to be taken, that a character doing such a thing may lose their mind to the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T12:29:12-07:00","id":1491020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490552-fairy-stricken-another-form-of-fairy-kidnapping#post1490552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a companion to my post of fairy stocks/fetches <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488496-fairy-stocks-fetches&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Another way for fairies to abduct people was not by kidnapping them physically, but ensnaring their souls or minds.<br /> <br /> There is lots of folklore of people being in some kind of immobile, comatose, or sickened state as having been taking by the fairies. But they didn't believe the sick, immobile person had been replaced. They believed the person's body was still there, but their mind had been transplanted into the fairy world where it was now trapped. (The medical term &amp;quot;stroke&amp;quot; in fact is derived from a person being &amp;quot;elf struck&amp;quot;.)<br /> <br /> This is also seen in a different degree in the book and BBC miniseries Jonathon Strange a &amp; Mr Norrel where Lady Pole is forced to attend fairy balls every night during her sleep, a process that gradually wastes her from exhaustion since she can never get rest.<br /> <br /> What would be a good way to emulate that? Now in the Enchanted rules, we do learn that enchanted humans who spend too much time in the Dreaming can become dream struck and fall into coma, but that isn't this. I've also used the term fairy stricken or association with actual strokes and similar medical trauma to describe the process of the Chrysalis, especially for Wilders and Grumps who change late. This is just a way for the fae to somehow take a person's soul or mind, incarnate in a (likely chimerical, but identical) body to serve them in the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> This is certainly something that should be beyond any normal Arts. But I can't think of some general mechanics that can emulate it, but have sufficient limitations that fairies just can't do it everyone. It should be relatively rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way that this could be accomplished would be by using the Infusion Art (with Actor, Fae and possibly Prop). Altering an enchanted mortal, perhaps replacing the victims &quot;heart&quot; with an enchanted thing (hornets nest, clockwork gadget, a gemstone etc). <br /> The fae enchanter might implant chimerical banes that impose all kinds of nastiness. Or the replacement part might be programmed to torment the hapless mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}